  "texts": {
    "preamble": "K.D.Sundaran vs Food Inspector on 22 February, 2016",
    "facts": "The prosecution allegation can be briefly stated thus:- On 22.05.2002 at about 5.00 p.m., PW1, the Food Inspector purchased 750 gram of peas dhal from the shop of the first accused. After sampling as per rules, one sample was sent to the Public Analyst for analysis. The Public Analyst, after analysis submitted Ext.P12 report stating that the sample did not conform to the standard prescribed for the food grain under the PFA Rules, 1955 and was therefore adulterated. It was also alleged that the first accused sold the food item without having a valid licence under the PFA Rules. 4. Before the trial Court, PW1 to PW4 were examined and Exts.P1 to P15 were marked for the prosecution. DW1 to DW3 were examined and Exts.D1 to D9 series were marked for the revision petitioner. The incident in this case was on 22.05.2002. There is no previous conviction against the revision petitioner. There is also no allegation that the revision petitioner was involved in any other offence of similar nature, after the incident in this case.",
    "arguments": "6. The learned counsel for the revision petitioner has submitted that the revision petitioner applied for the renewal of the licence subsequent to the incident in this case.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "6. The learned counsel for the revision petitioner has submitted that the revision petitioner applied for the renewal of the licence subsequent to the incident in this case.",
